practiceProblems.problemStatement:
Build a fleet system with:
1. A parent class `Vehicle` with `String model` and a method `void drive()` printing `model + " is moving on the road."`;
2. Subclass `Truck` extending `Vehicle` with `double cargoCapacityTons` and `void loadCargo()` printing `"Loading " + cargoCapacityTons + " tons into " + model`;
3. Subclass `Motorcycle` extending `Vehicle` with `boolean hasSidecar` and `void popWheelie()` printing `model + " pops a wheelie! (Sidecar: " + hasSidecar + ")"`;
In `Main.main()`, instantiate a `Truck` (`model = "Volvo FH", cargoCapacityTons = 18.5`) and call `drive()` then `loadCargo()`. Then instantiate a `Motorcycle` (`model = "Yamaha R1", hasSidecar = false`) and call `drive()` then `popWheelie()`.

practiceProblems.solutionCode:
class Vehicle {
    String model;

    void drive() {
        System.out.println(model + " is moving on the road.");
    }
}

class Truck extends Vehicle {
    double cargoCapacityTons;

    void loadCargo() {
        System.out.println("Loading " + cargoCapacityTons + " tons into " + model);
    }
}

class Motorcycle extends Vehicle {
    boolean hasSidecar;

    void popWheelie() {
        System.out.println(model + " pops a wheelie! (Sidecar: " + hasSidecar + ")");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Truck truck = new Truck();
        truck.model = "Volvo FH";
        truck.cargoCapacityTons = 18.5;
        truck.drive();
        truck.loadCargo();

        Motorcycle bike = new Motorcycle();
        bike.model = "Yamaha R1";
        bike.hasSidecar = false;
        bike.drive();
        bike.popWheelie();
    }
}
